hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"237","On the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Bishr bin al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Razzaq, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of al-Muttalib bin Abdullah bin Hantab, on the authority of Umm Hani, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was at the top of Mecca on the day of the Conquest, so I came to him, and Abu Dharr came With a bowl containing water, I said: I can see traces of dough in it. She said: So Abu Dharr covered him, so he took a bath. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, covered Abu He left his hair, took a bath, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed eight rak’ahs, and that was in the forenoon.”"
